=[ Manifest Reference ]

Generated by `catasto spec manifest` from Rust schema definitions in `crates/catasto-manifest/`. Do not edit it: change the doc comments there and run the command again.

Authoritative reference of all declarations and fields supported in `catasto.ctmt`.

==[ upstreams ]

Upstream repository definitions declared in `::upstreams`. An upstream declares a named Git repository at a pinned revision, optionally with a `root` directory inside the repository from which entry paths start.

- `git` (string): Repository URL (`https://` URL or workspace-relative path).
- `rev` (string, default: `main`): Pinned tag, branch, or commit hash. Quote numeric revisions (e.g. `rev: "1.2"`).
- `root` (path): Directory inside the upstream repository that entry paths are relative to.

==[ entry ]

Manifest file entry declaring a managed workspace file. Each top-level map entry in `catasto.ctmt` binds a workspace-relative file path to its canonical content origin (`source`).

- `source` (string | map): Where canonical content comes from: a local path string, or a map with `git`, `rev`, `path`, or `upstream`.
- `source.git` (string): Git repository URL (`https://` URL or workspace-relative local path).
- `source.rev` (string, default: `main`): Tag, branch, or commit hash. Quote numeric revisions (e.g. `rev: "1.2"`).
- `source.path` (path): Location of the file inside the upstream Git repository.
- `source.upstream` (string): Name of an upstream repository declared in `::upstreams`.
- `source.symlink` ("follow" | "keep", default: `follow`): Symlink preservation mode in git sources (`follow` to resolve target content, or `keep` to preserve symlink itself).
